---
title: "update_single_price_feed (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_version: latest_only = state::assert_latest_only(pyth_state)
    q_version --> q_fee_check: base_update_fee <= coin::value(fee)
    q_fee_check --> q_abort_fee: false, abort E_INSUFFICIENT_FEE
    q_fee_check --> q_deposit: true
    q_deposit --> q_init_search: price_info::deposit_fee_coins(price_info_object, fee)
    q_init_search --> q_loop: i = 0, found = false
    q_loop --> q_borrow: i < hot_potato_vector::length(price_updates)
    q_loop --> q_not_found: i >= length AND found == false
    q_borrow --> q_match: cur = borrow(price_updates, i)
    q_match --> q_update: has_same_price_identifier == true
    q_match --> q_inc: has_same_price_identifier == false
    q_update --> q_done: update_cache(latest_only, cur, price_info_object, clock), found = true
    q_inc --> q_loop: i = i + 1
    q_not_found --> q_abort_nf: abort E_PRICE_UPDATE_NOT_FOUND_FOR_PRICE_INFO_OBJECT
    q_done --> [*]: return price_updates

    note right of q_fee_check
        INV-001: fee must be >= base_update_fee (per individual update)
        INV-002: fee coins are deposited into the PriceInfoObject
        INV-003: exactly one matching price update must exist in the vector
        INV-004: HotPotatoVector is returned (not consumed) for further updates
    end note
